00:06:03.730 --> 00:06:07.150
- It's kinda weird to me that,
as a survival specialist,

00:06:07.150 --> 00:06:09.430
he makes no use of fire here.

00:06:09.430 --> 00:06:11.240
Fire was invented for a reason,

00:06:11.240 --> 00:06:13.790
to cook things, to prevent infections,

00:06:13.790 --> 00:06:16.600
because one of the leading
killers before fire,

00:06:16.600 --> 00:06:18.360
before the use of cooking our food,

00:06:18.360 --> 00:06:20.480
storing our food correctly, was diarrhea.

00:06:20.480 --> 00:06:21.610
It would dehydrate you.

00:06:21.610 --> 00:06:22.860
Electrolyte imbalance.

00:06:22.860 --> 00:06:23.693
Your heart would stop.

00:06:23.693 --> 00:06:24.800
Acute kidney failure.

00:06:24.800 --> 00:06:26.970
- [Bear] I've noticed a
lot of bees in the area,

00:06:26.970 --> 00:06:28.450
so I'm heading through the scrub

00:06:28.450 --> 00:06:30.430
to get to the hive and find some honey.

00:06:30.430 --> 00:06:31.800
- You know I'm a honey fan.

00:06:31.800 --> 00:06:33.060
Like, I love honey.

00:06:33.060 --> 00:06:34.790
Honey works as good, or better,

00:06:34.790 --> 00:06:36.710
than over-the-counter cough suppressants

00:06:36.710 --> 00:06:38.161
in the pediatric population.

00:06:38.161 --> 00:06:42.060
(tense music)
(bees buzzing)

00:06:42.060 --> 00:06:43.540
Oh, that looks fresh.

00:06:43.540 --> 00:06:45.370
Fresh honeycomb.

00:06:45.370 --> 00:06:48.350
- [Bear] Leaving my forehead
exposed was a real oversight.

00:06:48.350 --> 00:06:50.720
- If you get a really bad sting,

00:06:50.720 --> 00:06:52.270
and you happen to be an individual

00:06:52.270 --> 00:06:54.620
who is severely allergic to a bee sting,

00:06:54.620 --> 00:06:55.790
you go into anaphylactic shock,

00:06:55.790 --> 00:06:57.950
where your throat closes up,
your blood pressure drops.

00:06:57.950 --> 00:07:00.270
That could be lethal very, very quickly.

00:07:00.270 --> 00:07:02.330
That's why if you know
you have an allergy,

00:07:02.330 --> 00:07:05.080
you should have an EpiPen, like
that, on hand at all times,

00:07:05.080 --> 00:07:06.080
and not necessarily an EpiPen,

00:07:06.080 --> 00:07:08.570
any kind of epinephrine autoinjector.

00:07:08.570 --> 00:07:10.840
Oh, he's swelling.

00:07:10.840 --> 00:07:12.910
- The bee sting has made all of, you know,

00:07:12.910 --> 00:07:13.743
this part of me swell up.

00:07:13.743 --> 00:07:14.580
Allergic reactions can be fatal.

00:07:14.580 --> 00:07:16.810
- That's serious edema right there.

00:07:16.810 --> 00:07:19.090
- I'm worried about anaphylactic shock,

00:07:19.090 --> 00:07:21.600
the first signs of
swelling around the eyes,

00:07:21.600 --> 00:07:24.760
followed by difficulty breathing
and loss of consciousness.

00:07:24.760 --> 00:07:27.700
- These type of large
reactions are really treated

00:07:27.700 --> 00:07:30.550
with supportive care if it's
not true anaphylactic shock.

00:07:30.550 --> 00:07:32.040
You wanna think cold compresses,

00:07:32.040 --> 00:07:33.920
steroids in serious cases,

00:07:33.920 --> 00:07:35.300
and really just making sure

00:07:35.300 --> 00:07:37.510
that the patient's
airway's not compromised,

00:07:37.510 --> 00:07:39.240
their blood pressure remains stable.

00:07:39.240 --> 00:07:42.810
Once that's okay, that usually
does pass in a few days.

00:07:42.810 --> 00:07:46.040
But swelling on its own, if
it's not over the airway,

00:07:46.040 --> 00:07:47.900
is not intrinsically dangerous.

00:07:47.900 --> 00:07:50.320
- [Bear] I'm on a raft
in the Pacific Ocean.

00:07:50.320 --> 00:07:51.987
I've collected some fresh water,

00:07:51.987 --> 00:07:54.710
but it's full of bird
droppings and it's rancid.

00:07:54.710 --> 00:07:56.670
Drink this, and you'd probably vomit,

00:07:56.670 --> 00:07:58.830
and risk worsening dehydration.

00:07:58.830 --> 00:08:01.010
But there is a way of using it

00:08:01.010 --> 00:08:02.860
to gain life-giving fluids,

00:08:02.860 --> 00:08:04.440
but only as a last resort.

00:08:04.440 --> 00:08:05.673
- I don't even know what he's about to do,

00:08:05.673 --> 00:08:08.680
but the fact that it has
bird droppings makes me think

00:08:08.680 --> 00:08:10.130
that there's so much E. coli in it,

00:08:10.130 --> 00:08:12.770
that if it makes any contact
with the inside of your body,

00:08:12.770 --> 00:08:14.490
whether it's through a
cut or you drinking it,

00:08:14.490 --> 00:08:16.210
you're just gonna get a massive infection.

00:08:16.210 --> 00:08:17.370
And a massive infection,

00:08:17.370 --> 00:08:19.380
when you're stranded
and you're surviving is,

00:08:19.380 --> 00:08:21.760
like, the worst case scenario.

00:08:21.760 --> 00:08:23.304
- [Bear] I'm gonna give myself an enema.

00:08:23.304 --> 00:08:25.700
- (laughs) Oh, my God!

00:08:25.700 --> 00:08:27.240
He doesn't try and survive.

00:08:27.240 --> 00:08:28.073
He's gotta think,

00:08:28.073 --> 00:08:31.320
"What is the most ridiculous,
extreme thing I can do

00:08:31.320 --> 00:08:32.650
in order to make this show?"

00:08:32.650 --> 00:08:35.380
Could you absorb fluids from your rectum?

00:08:35.380 --> 00:08:37.440
Yes, there are small blood vessels there.

00:08:37.440 --> 00:08:38.900
We do give suppositories there,

00:08:38.900 --> 00:08:41.630
so there are absorptive qualities there.

00:08:41.630 --> 00:08:43.270
Oh, my God, I can't believe
I'm even thinking about this.

00:08:43.270 --> 00:08:45.800
There's also a lot of bacteria
that lives in your rectum,

00:08:45.800 --> 00:08:49.460
including E. coli, which
doesn't enter your bloodstream.

00:08:49.460 --> 00:08:52.160
So, it could be an okay
place to have some bacteria.

00:08:52.160 --> 00:08:54.630
There's just so much that could go wrong.

00:08:54.630 --> 00:08:56.170
I think it's, like, a 50/50 shot.

00:08:56.170 --> 00:08:59.584
Will you survive, or will
you kill yourself further?

00:08:59.584 --> 00:09:02.390
- Now, that's placenta.

00:09:02.390 --> 00:09:03.223
- Oh, my God.

00:09:03.223 --> 00:09:04.860
- Did somebody have a baby?
- Is that Shaq?

00:09:04.860 --> 00:09:07.190
- What's rare, though,
is find it so fresh.

00:09:07.190 --> 00:09:09.260
That, for me, is good news.

00:09:09.260 --> 00:09:10.180
- Is it good news?

00:09:10.180 --> 00:09:12.020
- [Bear] It looks, actually, like dinner.

00:09:12.020 --> 00:09:13.480
- Shaq, don't do it, buddy.

00:09:13.480 --> 00:09:14.860
I've seen you three-peat.

00:09:14.860 --> 00:09:18.193
- And this is a first
for me, to eat placenta.

00:09:19.510 --> 00:09:21.373
- Yeah, it should be a last.

00:09:23.208 --> 00:09:24.870
(placenta sizzles)

00:09:24.870 --> 00:09:26.420
Like, there are some
cultures that do this,

00:09:26.420 --> 00:09:29.020
because the placenta is,
like, it has the nutrients,

00:09:29.020 --> 00:09:31.160
and it does the oxygen distribution

00:09:31.160 --> 00:09:32.990
for the baby through the umbilical cord,

00:09:32.990 --> 00:09:34.810
and there's some cultures
that think about doing this.

00:09:34.810 --> 00:09:37.350
But, like, the CDC has put
out a specific warning,

00:09:37.350 --> 00:09:38.330
like, do not do this.

00:09:38.330 --> 00:09:41.650
If you get a group B strep
infection in your placenta,

00:09:41.650 --> 00:09:42.483
and then you eat it,

00:09:42.483 --> 00:09:44.170
and then you pass it to your
baby through breast milk,

00:09:44.170 --> 00:09:45.003
that's deadly.

00:09:45.003 --> 00:09:46.180
That's lethal to a newborn.

00:09:49.230 --> 00:09:50.490
I give him props.

00:09:50.490 --> 00:09:51.919
I wouldn't do it.

00:09:51.919 --> 00:09:54.430
(Shaq spits)
- (laughs) Shaq is my man.

00:09:54.430 --> 00:09:56.740
- [Bear] It's traditional for Berber men

00:09:56.740 --> 00:09:58.800
to eat goats' testicles.

00:09:58.800 --> 00:10:00.840
They're thought to enhance fertility,

00:10:00.840 --> 00:10:03.220
and it's certainly gonna
be a test of my manhood.

00:10:03.220 --> 00:10:05.030
- Look, I'm respective of all cultures.

00:10:05.030 --> 00:10:07.410
The line I draw is medical misinformation.

00:10:07.410 --> 00:10:09.330
If you're gonna tell
me eating a goat's nut

00:10:09.330 --> 00:10:11.580
is gonna help you get fertile,

00:10:11.580 --> 00:10:12.510
I'm not gonna buy it.

00:10:12.510 --> 00:10:14.683
I need evidence-based medicine for that.

00:10:17.430 --> 00:10:18.263
Why raw?

00:10:18.263 --> 00:10:20.010
Just put it over a flame.

00:10:20.010 --> 00:10:22.501
- [Bear] Well, that's
definitely a first for me.

00:10:22.501 --> 00:10:24.080
(Bear retching)
- See, he's throwing up,

00:10:24.080 --> 00:10:26.140
because there's bacteria and it's gross.

00:10:26.140 --> 00:10:29.100
- And what this stuff
is, is like sunblock.

00:10:29.100 --> 00:10:29.950
- Oh, wow.

00:10:29.950 --> 00:10:32.500
- And the coral, itself,
we use, it's at low tide.

00:10:32.500 --> 00:10:34.210
When it's exposed to the sun,

00:10:34.210 --> 00:10:37.100
it will secrete this as a
way of protecting itself.

00:10:37.100 --> 00:10:38.500
Just amazing.
- Wow.

00:10:38.500 --> 00:10:40.870
- Scientists have actually
reckoned this stuff

00:10:40.870 --> 00:10:42.670
is as good as factor 50.

00:10:42.670 --> 00:10:45.150
- Wow, an SPF 50's
pretty great protection.

00:10:45.150 --> 00:10:47.730
I mean, I always say get
the highest SPF possible,

00:10:47.730 --> 00:10:50.470
even though once you get above
50, not much is changing.

00:10:50.470 --> 00:10:52.840
That's only if you're
following the exact guidelines,

00:10:52.840 --> 00:10:54.907
and I don't know about
this whole mushroom thing,

00:10:54.907 --> 00:10:56.830
but just get the one from the store.

00:10:56.830 --> 00:10:58.910
- [Bear] If it's got tentacles like that,

00:10:58.910 --> 00:11:00.460
those are stingers.

00:11:00.460 --> 00:11:01.610
But--
- So you can't eat it?

00:11:01.610 --> 00:11:02.606
- Jellyfish scare me.

00:11:02.606 --> 00:11:04.020
- You can eat the body of it.
- Right.

00:11:04.020 --> 00:11:04.853
- Foil it out.

00:11:04.853 --> 00:11:06.783
And it's a bit like,

00:11:06.783 --> 00:11:08.220
tastes a little bit like gelatine.

00:11:08.220 --> 00:11:09.400
It's pure protein.

00:11:09.400 --> 00:11:11.270
- I don't know what the deal
is with eating jellyfish.

00:11:11.270 --> 00:11:13.820
I missed that day in
residency in a medical school.

00:11:13.820 --> 00:11:16.490
Folks, today, we're learning
about eating jellyfish.

00:11:16.490 --> 00:11:18.808
It's like peanut butter
and jelly, but with fish.

00:11:18.808 --> 00:11:20.161
- And those are the,

00:11:20.161 --> 00:11:20.994
those,

00:11:20.994 --> 00:11:22.451
(Bear yelps)

00:11:22.451 --> 00:11:24.220
- It got you?
- Yeah.

00:11:24.220 --> 00:11:25.480
- So he got stung by a jellyfish,

00:11:25.480 --> 00:11:26.810
- Oh! He put it in his mouth?

00:11:26.810 --> 00:11:27.643
- I've seen movies before

00:11:27.643 --> 00:11:29.440
where if somebody gets
stung by a jellyfish,

00:11:29.440 --> 00:11:30.310
you have to pee on them.

00:11:30.310 --> 00:11:32.500
- The whole thing with
peeing on a jellyfish sting,

00:11:32.500 --> 00:11:36.270
really comes from preventing
the discharge of more toxin,

00:11:36.270 --> 00:11:37.760
and creating more inflammation.

00:11:37.760 --> 00:11:39.950
The general consensus has
been to use sea water,

00:11:39.950 --> 00:11:41.920
and not to use fresh water, especially,

00:11:41.920 --> 00:11:44.040
'cause it can cause more of
that toxin to be released.

00:11:44.040 --> 00:11:46.380
- If you just relax, then I'll relax,

00:11:46.380 --> 00:11:47.640
now I've got stage fright.

00:11:47.640 --> 00:11:49.420
- I can't relax.

00:11:49.420 --> 00:11:51.780
- To pee on demand when
somebody is in pain

00:11:51.780 --> 00:11:53.010
is very difficult.

00:11:53.010 --> 00:11:55.940
- Peeing is actually a
complex, neurologic process.

00:11:55.940 --> 00:11:57.490
It's very easy to throw that off.

00:11:57.490 --> 00:11:59.700
If, for example, you've had a stroke,

00:11:59.700 --> 00:12:00.890
if you've had an injury to that area,

00:12:00.890 --> 00:12:04.350
it's very easy to develop
urinary incontinence,

00:12:04.350 --> 00:12:06.440
or urinary retention, and sometimes,

00:12:06.440 --> 00:12:08.950
the treatment for that,
is actually biofeedback,

00:12:08.950 --> 00:12:12.100
and understanding how to
control different muscles

00:12:12.100 --> 00:12:12.933
in the area.

00:12:12.933 --> 00:12:16.580
- I've been in water this cold before.

00:12:16.580 --> 00:12:17.943
- Oh, he's going swimming in cold water.

00:12:17.943 --> 00:12:19.640
- It's plain horrible.

00:12:19.640 --> 00:12:21.630
- Yeah, it's horrible
just getting undressed.

00:12:21.630 --> 00:12:23.103
- Chilly Perkins.

00:12:23.960 --> 00:12:26.740
Okay. Well, I'm hooked up to
this transmitter, as well,

00:12:26.740 --> 00:12:28.860
and that should show you my heart rate,

00:12:28.860 --> 00:12:30.310
but also, my breathing rate.

00:12:30.310 --> 00:12:31.300
- Generally what happens is,

00:12:31.300 --> 00:12:33.280
when you hit really cold
temperatures like that,

00:12:33.280 --> 00:12:34.230
or go under water,

00:12:34.230 --> 00:12:36.470
lot of times you'll
have this diving reflex,

00:12:36.470 --> 00:12:38.600
where your body will
automatically send you

00:12:38.600 --> 00:12:40.040
into a bradycardic rhythm,

00:12:40.040 --> 00:12:41.730
where the electrical
activity of your heart

00:12:41.730 --> 00:12:44.387
actually slows down,
to allow you to survive

00:12:44.387 --> 00:12:46.110
longer under water.

00:12:46.110 --> 00:12:47.630
We actually used to use
this type of treatment

00:12:47.630 --> 00:12:49.470
for supraventricular tachycardia,

00:12:49.470 --> 00:12:51.350
where we actually got patients to perform

00:12:51.350 --> 00:12:53.420
this diving reflex, vagal maneuver,

00:12:53.420 --> 00:12:56.010
and it would reset their
heart rhythm, slow it down.

00:12:56.010 --> 00:12:58.110
Obviously needs to be
very carefully monitored.

00:12:58.110 --> 00:13:00.140
And now, with the new medications
that we have on board,

00:13:00.140 --> 00:13:03.016
we generally don't have to do this.

00:13:03.016 --> 00:13:05.820
(water splashes)
Oh! I'm cold for him.

00:13:05.820 --> 00:13:07.570
I'm cold for him!

00:13:07.570 --> 00:13:09.290
- [Bear] Watch, as my heart rate drops

00:13:09.290 --> 00:13:12.190
from 160 beats per minute to 55.

00:13:12.190 --> 00:13:13.300
- Yep, diving reflex.

00:13:13.300 --> 00:13:15.300
- It's known as a mammalian dive reflex.

00:13:15.300 --> 00:13:19.260
It gives you vital, extra
seconds to make it for surface.

00:13:19.260 --> 00:13:21.300
- He did it! See, it worked,

00:13:21.300 --> 00:13:22.750
his survival mechanism kicked in.

00:13:22.750 --> 00:13:26.130
We also actually use hypothermia
treatment in patients

00:13:26.130 --> 00:13:28.650
who are undergoing
prolonged cardiac arrest,

00:13:28.650 --> 00:13:30.400
where we realize that
if we put them through

00:13:30.400 --> 00:13:32.380
a hypothermia protocol, very controlled,

00:13:32.380 --> 00:13:35.640
we actually decrease the
oxygen demand on the body,

00:13:35.640 --> 00:13:36.690
on certain organs,

00:13:36.690 --> 00:13:40.060
therefore we give them a little
bit longer survival time.

00:13:40.060 --> 00:13:42.080
Bear Grylls certainly
does a lot of cool stuff

00:13:42.080 --> 00:13:42.913
on the ground,

00:13:42.913 --> 00:13:45.270
but I just flew an F-16 in the sky,

00:13:45.270 --> 00:13:47.320
here's what happens to your
body when you're flying

00:13:47.320 --> 00:13:49.560
in an F-16 and experiencing a lot of G's.

